	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Feralas is the great green wilderness of south-western {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. Its forests are tall and wet, its rivers wide, and two great pillars of stone, the {link:the-twin-colossals}Twin Colossals{/link}, rise above its northern hills. Giants walk its northern hills. Hippogryphs nest on its southern heights, and faerie dragons flit through its glades. Under the trees lie the ruins of an elder age, and at the forest's heart stand the broken halls of Eldre'Thalas, the city of the {red:highborne}Highborne{/red} now called {red:dire-maul}Dire Maul{/red}. It is one of the last wild places of Kalimdor, and both the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} have come to claim it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Long ago this forest belonged to the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link}. Their pavilions, towers and shrines still stand in ruin across it, from the {link:ruins-of-solarsal}Ruins of Solarsal{/link} on the coast to the fallen stones of the {link:high-wilderness}High Wilderness{/link}. The greatest of their works was Eldre'Thalas. It survived the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, but its prince, {red:tortheldrin}Tortheldrin{/red}, fed his people's thirst for magic with ever darker powers. Some of his subjects rose against him. They lost, and fled west across the sea, and their descendants are the {link:skyborne}Skyborne{/link} of {link:zephras-isle}Zephras Isle{/link}. The city that remained sank slowly into ruin. No chronicle records when the last kaldorei left the rest of Feralas, or why.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[After the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, General {link:shandris-feathermoon}Shandris Feathermoon{/link} led an expedition of the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} into Feralas and made {link:feathermoon-stronghold}Feathermoon Stronghold{/link}, on an island off its western coast, her seat. Her purpose is plain. The Sentinel Army holds back the {link:horde}Horde{/link} in {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link} and the {link:stonetalon-mountains}Stonetalon Mountains{/link}, and she will not let the Horde take the last wild lands behind them. The Horde has come anyway. {link:tauren}Tauren{/link}, orcs and trolls hold {link:camp-mojache}Camp Mojache{/link} in the east, between the ogres to the north and the gnolls to the south.

Neither side is the land's only enemy. The Gordunni ogres scar the forest wherever they settle. The Hatecrest {link:naga}naga{/link} dig in the coastal ruins for something no one understands. The Grimtotem tauren trap faerie dragons, and the Woodpaw gnolls grow more desperate each season. Their desperation has a cause. In the south-east, in a place called the {link:the-writhing-deep}Writhing Deep{/link}, insects out of {link:silithus}Silithus{/link} have built a hive, and they are spreading.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} of {link:feathermoon-stronghold}Feathermoon{/link}.{/b} Night elf warriors, druids, priestesses and scholars under {link:shandris-feathermoon}Shandris Feathermoon{/link}.
• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link} of {link:camp-mojache}Camp Mojache{/link}.{/b} {link:tauren}Tauren{/link} hunters, {link:orcs}orc{/link} warriors and troll witch doctors, holding the eastern forest.
• {b}The Gordunni ogres.{/b} A tribe that holds the lands north of Camp Mojache and the ruins of the {link:high-wilderness}High Wilderness{/link}.
• {b}The Hatecrest {link:naga}naga{/link}.{/b} Serpent-folk of the western coast, the {link:isle-of-dread}Isle of Dread{/link} and the {link:ruins-of-solarsal}Ruins of Solarsal{/link}.
• {b}The Northspring harpies.{/b} They roost in the {link:ruins-of-ravenwind}Ruins of Ravenwind{/link} in the north-west.
• {b}The Woodpaw gnolls.{/b} Their camps fill the hills south of Camp Mojache.
• {b}The {link:grimtotem-clan}Grimtotem{/link}.{/b} Tauren who reject {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link}, camped in the eastern forest.
• {b}The Zukk'ash.{/b} Insects of the silithid kind, in the {link:the-writhing-deep}Writhing Deep{/link}.
• {b}The creatures of the wild.{/b} Mountain giants, treants, hippogryphs, sprite darters, yetis, groddoc apes and ironfur bears.
• {b}The green dragonkin.{/b} Guardians of the {link:dream-bough}Dream Bough{/link} in the north, the gate of the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Elven Age.{/b} The night elves and the Highborne built across the forest. Eldre'Thalas was their crown.
• {b}The Rebellion of Eldre'Thalas.{/b} After the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, rebels rose against Prince Tortheldrin and fled into the sky. The prince kept his city.
• {b}The Long Silence.{/b} For ages the forest was left to beasts, ogres and ruin.
• {b}The Coming of the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link}.{/b} After the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:shandris-feathermoon}Shandris Feathermoon{/link} brought her expedition south and made {link:feathermoon-stronghold}Feathermoon Stronghold{/link} its bastion.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The {link:horde}Horde{/link} holds {link:camp-mojache}Camp Mojache{/link}. {link:naga}Naga{/link}, ogres, harpies and gnolls press on every side, and a hive of insects grows in the south.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Wilds",
			text = [=[• The trolls of {link:camp-mojache}Camp Mojache{/link} say that a beast slain by violence leaves behind its muisek, a spirit that may escape and return in a greater and more vengeful shape.
• Scholars who come from {link:thousand-needles}Thousand Needles{/link} remark that the green of Feralas ends at the canyons as sharply as a drawn line.
• A book called {i}Feralas: A History{/i} is kept by a lore keeper of {link:rut-theran-village}Rut'theran Village{/link}, beneath {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}. By her account, whatever was truly valuable in the ruins was carried off long ago by ogres and harpies.
• A goblin engineer of the {link:the-forgotten-coast}Forgotten Coast{/link} calls it the worst place in the world to open a shop.]=],
		},
	},
})

